  ## Minor Crimes
  - Warnings must be issued for a first offense of a Minor crime.
  - If multiple minor crimes have been committed or the crime constitutes a repeat offense, then 5 minutes is the maximum sentence for a Minor crime (with the exception of Failure to Comply).
  <Table Columns="4">
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Offense
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Description
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Notes
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Code
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#593a4e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Failure to Comply (E)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To fail to comply with a lawful order from a commanding authority.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        A person may only be charged with this crime if the relevant authority has made a complaint. Minor failures to follow Space Law by Command or Security are also included in this crime. A person may not be sentenced with Confinement for this crime, only Warning or Demotion.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-00
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#2e422e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Petty Theft (H)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To take non-vital or inexpensive property of another individual, organization, or common property, without
        consent.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Petty theft covers the possession of items that were not lawfully or consensually given to the holder.
        This includes departmentally restricted items, if the item was not approved for the holder.
        Items covered by petty theft are usually easily replaceable, low-value, or low-danger.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-01
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#453a59">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Vandalism (D)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To intentionally deface or superficially damage public or private property.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Painting inappropriate graffiti, smashing bar glasses, breaking lights, or eating a crewmember's plushie is vandalism, breaking a window into
        space or secure areas is not.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-02
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#59563a">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Trespass (T)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To enter a non-secure area without permission.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        It is best to just remove them from the area unless this is a repeat offense.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-03
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Animal Cruelty (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To inflict unnecessary suffering or harm on a non-sapient being with malicious intent.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This doesn't include legitimate and authorized animal testing and usually doesn't extend to vermin such as mice, animals normally used in the process of food production, or creatures that could pose a threat to the station.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-04
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Endangerment (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To recklessly put yourself or others in danger, either through direct action or failure to act.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Covers industrial accidents, industrial negligence, self-experimentation, or even medical malpractice.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-05
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#3b4354">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Disturbance (R)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To cause a public disturbance.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Sometimes referred to as hooliganism. The catch-all for obnoxious crewmates. Covers things such as public
        nudity, needless insults, obstructing authorities, and inciting crime or violence.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        1-06
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
  </Table>

  ## Moderate Crimes
  - The maximum sentence for a Moderate crime is 5 minutes.
  <Table Columns="4">
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Offense
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Description
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Notes
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Code
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#593a4e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Resisting a Lawful Search (E)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To resist a reasonable or lawful search or seizure by a member of the security department, or an authorized head of staff.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        The search or seizure must be legal per Space Law.
        The perpetrator must have made an active attempt to flee, resist restraint or search, or, if applicable, refuse to hand over contraband.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-00
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#2e422e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Grand Theft (H)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To take critical or unreplaceable property of another individual or organization without consent.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        The difference between theft and grand theft is based on how crucial the stolen item is; this is mostly
        used for the theft of command staff items – items such as door remotes, hardsuits, jetpacks, and irreplaceable
        machine parts. Additionally, theft of anything from the armory is grand theft.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-01
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#453a59">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Damage of Property (D)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To maliciously damage or deface public or private property or equipment.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This includes destruction of job equipment, such as hydro trays, booze dispensers, and chemical dispensers. It is a step up from
        vandalism but a step down from critical property destruction.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-02
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#59563a">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Secure Trespass (T)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To enter a secured area without permission.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This covers areas such as telecommunications, Security, and Command-restricted areas.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-03
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Assault (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To threaten to or to use physical force against a member of the crew without the intent to kill.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Attempted murder and assault are different. A fist fight is most likely assault; A shooting may be an
        attempted murder. Ensure that all required context is obtained before discerning the difference.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-04
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Gross Negligence (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        A conscious, reckless disregard for the safety or well-being of others.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This entails causing an unreasonable amount of damage to a part of the station as a result of negligence, such as purposefully allowing anomalies to go critical, or causing an accidental but not permanent death.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        2-05
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
  </Table>

  ## Major Crimes
  - The maximum sentence for a Major crime is 10 minutes.
  <Table Columns="4">
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Offense
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Description
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Notes
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Code
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#593a4e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Obstruction of Justice (E)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To intentionally impede or otherwise prevent a member of the security department from enforcing the law.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This applies to attempting to prevent an officer from making a lawful arrest, detention, or execution, among other instances.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        3-00
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#453a59">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Minor Sabotage/Destruction (D)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To cause minor damage to an area or a minor station system.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This includes the destruction of station machinery such as ID card computers, telecommunications servers,
        power devices such as substations, and non-hostile silicon units.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        3-02
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Kidnapping (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To unlawfully restrain, transport, control, or confine a sapient being against that individual’s will.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This covers a large range of offenses, used mostly as a catch-all when dealing with unlawful control of another being.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        3-04
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#3b4354">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Rioting (R)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To take part in a large group of personnel creating an unlawful public disturbance.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Leaders of a riot may be charged with all crimes that happen under their leadership.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        3-06
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
  </Table>

  ## Extreme Crimes
  - The maximum sentence for an extreme crime is 15 minutes.
  <Table Columns="4">
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Offense
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Description
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Notes
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Code
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#593a4e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Breach of Custody (E)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To break out of a cell or custody with the intention of escaping.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This does not include breaking out due to threat of life or limb against the person.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        4-00
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#453a59">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Major Sabotage/Destruction (D)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To cause massive damage to an area or major station system.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This is mostly used for deadly departmental bombings or sabotage of major station systems
        such as the TEG or the ATS.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        4-02
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Attempted Murder (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To try to use force against a crewmember with the clear intent to kill.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This covers Attempt to and Intention to Commit Murder.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        4-04
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Manslaughter (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To incidentally kill a crewmember without intent.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This includes manslaughter in both self-defense and negligent manslaughter.
        If there is provable intent, then the subject should instead be charged with (attempted) murder.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        4-05
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
  </Table>

  ## Capital Crimes
  - Capital crimes carry Capital sentences: permanent confinement, execution, or DNR.
  <Table Columns="4">
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Offense
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Description
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Notes
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box>
        Code
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#593a4e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Breach of Permanent Confinement (E)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To break someone sentenced to permanent confinement out of a cell or custody with the intention of escaping.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        If the person convicted of this crime was previously sentenced to permanent confinement, Execution or DNR must instead be carried out.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        5-00
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#453a59">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Station-Wide Destruction (D)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To engage in maliciously destructive actions which threaten to destroy, or successfully destroy a vessel or habitat.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Summed up, this is extreme sabotage of station systems or setting off self-destruction systems. This includes any method that causes the
        entire station to become uninhabitable, releasing an active singularity, station-wide atmospherics sabotage, and destruction of the station AI, among other offenses.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        5-02
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Murder (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To permanently kill a member of the crew.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This covers any successful attempt to kill a member of the crew and prevent resuscitation.
        If the victim was declared legally dead, but was able to be resuscitated, then it is only Attempted Murder. Eggshell skull doctrine applies here.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        5-04
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#4d2e2e">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Mass Acts of Violence (V)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To attempt to kill three or more sapient beings.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Applies when there have been three or more (Attempted) Murders with the intention to kill,
        or if the perpetrator has committed three or more acts of Manslaughter.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        5-05
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox Color="#3b4354">
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        Refusal of Mental Shielding (R)
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        To refuse to comply with a reasonable Mind Shielding procedure.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
      <Box HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="2">
        This applies if the suspect is excessively uncooperative or the implant fails to function due to the mental state of the prisoner already being too far gone.
        If the implant fails, they must be sentenced with Execution or DNR.
      </Box>
    </ColorBox>
    <ColorBox>
